 "about": "Exact single-locus Kingman branch-length moments at n = 8 (constant N, pair-coalescence rate 1, time in 2*N_ref generations), as rationals 'p/q': E_Li[i] = E[L_i] = 2/i; E_LiLj['i,j'] = E[L_i L_j], 1 <= i <= j <= 7, L_i = total branch length subtending i samples; pool_pairs = E_LiLj normalized over i <= j (= popcorn.twolocus.pool_pairs of the symmetric matrix); E_L2_analytic = E[(sum_i L_i)^2] = 4*sum_{j<n} 1/j^2 + (2*sum_{j<n} 1/j)^2. Derived by exact-rational dynamic programming over the Kingman jump chain and reproduced entry for entry by the closed form E[L_i L_j] = 4*sigma_ij + 4/(i*j), sigma_ij of Fu (1995). The rho = 0 limit of the two-locus E[T_i^A T_j^B]; comparand of the twolocus_kingman leg.",
